        "text": "Artificial intelligence technology is rapidly being updated and developed in the fields of products and services, and its application scope is gradually expanding. Among them, AI chatbots, an intelligent algorithm program providing chat and voice interaction functions, are one of the fastest-developing branches of artificial intelligence. [28]. Unlike a manual system, chatbots offer responses consistently and ask questions more quickly and efficiently. Chatbot is a kind of software that interacts with humans. It is mainly the update of the algorithmic language model, which rapidly promotes human-computer interaction. Natural Language Processing (NLP) is essential as the core technology in language learning interaction. NLP created an intelligent chatbot by generating answers through a pattern-matching program. Over the years, artificial intelligence chatbots with different functions and types have been created and developed. This includes text-to-text, text-to-speech, and speech-tospeech models [29]. Artificial Intelligence (AI) intelligent chatbots provide transformative learning tools for the entire educational environment. This technology provides learners personalized learning schemes and real-time feedback and interaction functions. AI chatbots provide language learners with a more personalized and interactive learning experience, especially in oral practice for EFL learners, which has garnered increasing attention. Zhang and Ardasheva [30] found that the improvement in EFL learners' self-efficacy during oral English practice is closely linked to a personalized learning experience, further emphasizing the potential of AI chatbots in fostering personalized learning. Additionally, research by An et al. [31] indicates that technology-assisted self-regulated language learning (TASRLL) can significantly enhance learners' motivation and learning outcomes in the oral practice environment for EFL learners. \n\nThe study found that using AI chatbots for