        "text": "However, these studies often focus on college learners, involve small sample sizes, and lack sufficient exploration of various language learning skills. One notable study investigated the effect of an AI-based technology platform on reading comprehension in Indian government schools, revealing a 70 percent improvement in learning outcomes, although variations were observed across states and grades (Srinivasan & Murthy, 2021). Despite its promising findings, the study's limited generalizability, reliance on self-administered assessments, and failure to analyze the impact on student characteristics point to the need for further research into the effectiveness of AI in enhancing reading comprehension across diverse contexts. \n\nConsidering these gaps, it is crucial for both researchers and educators to remain informed about the evolving and prospective applications of AI technologies in L2 reading instruction (Huang et al., 2023). This study seeks to explore the effectiveness of AI in advancing language learners' reading comprehension, fostering engagement, and promoting self-regulated learning. Specifically, the study explores AI-enhanced classrooms, where AI technologies and tools are integrated to support and optimize the teaching and learning process. The aim is to boost student engagement, improve learning outcomes, and create more effective and efficient educational experiences for both students and educators.",
