        "text": "This study provides evidence supporting the efficacy of the RTM platform, an AI-based intervention, in reinforcing reading comprehension and enhancing engagement between language learners. RTM include assessing the presence of AI-based features, such as natural language processing and machine learning algorithms, that enable personalized content delivery and adaptive feedback. Additionally, examining intelligent decisionmaking processes, such as adjusting difficulty levels or providing targeted recommendations, can indicate AI involvement. The ability of the RTM application to personalize the learning experience and adapt to individual learner needs, as well as its natural language understanding and generation capabilities, further support its classification as an AI intervention. Reviewing relevant documentation and technical specifications can provide valuable insights into the AI elements embedded in the RTM application. The results suggest that the use of AI-based platforms can be an effective way to foster selfregulated learning skills and enhance engagement in language learning. The personalized and interactive nature of the platform, combined with AI-based interventions, provided learners with an engaging and supportive learning environment. The findings of this study have important implications for language educators and suggest that integrating AI-based interventions into language learning can lead to more effective and efficient language learning outcomes. Further research is needed to explore the potential of AI-based platforms in supporting language learning and to identify best practices for their integration into language learning environments. \n\nThis study offers various implications for educators, practitioners, and students within the field of education. First, educators can utilize AI tools to improve reading comprehension and promote self-regulated learning among students. Through the use of AI tools, educators can offer personalized feedback and assistance to students, aiding them in enhancing their reading skills and fostering greater autonomy in their learning. This approach has the potential to improve student outcomes and enhance the effectiveness of teaching. Secondly, practitioners can gain from integrating AI into their instructional strategies. AI can offer real-time insights into student performance, enabling practitioners to pinpoint areas where students require additional support and adapt their teaching methods as needed. This approach can result in more efficient teaching and enhanced student outcomes. Additionally, students can benefit from AI interventions that strengthen their reading comprehension skills. AI tools can offer students tailored feedback, enabling them to monitor their progress and recognize areas where further support may be required.",
