      "snippet": {
        "text": "Artificial intelligence (AI) presents numerous benefits and limitations in enhancing digital literacy skills. AI language learning tools offer personalized learning experiences, increase learning speed, and introduce learners to different cultures (De la Vall et al., 2023). Additionally, AI can personalize learning, making it more inclusive for individuals with diverse cultural backgrounds (Chiu et al., 2023). However, challenges include the need for more human interaction, nuances in language contexts, and reliance on substantial data for training AI systems (De la Vall et al., 2023). Furthermore, AI can facilitate teachers' work and help students creatively solve educational problems (Tkachenko, 2023). Individuals must develop AI literacy skills to critically evaluate digital technologies and utilize them effectively in various settings (Kasinidou, 2023). Generative AI, a form of AI that can write, also plays a significant role in literacy teaching and learning, requiring a revised \"grammar\" for literacy in the age of AI (Kalantzis & Cope, 2023).",
