      "snippet": {
        "text": "Artificial Intelligence (AI) has emerged as a transformative force in digital literacy, offering innovative solutions to enhance learning experiences and address educational disparities. Integrating AI in digital literacy initiatives presents significant opportunities and challenges, particularly for underserved communities and diverse learning environments. AI holds considerable potential to improve digital literacy among underprivileged communities by addressing various barriers and leveraging tailored educational strategies. Community development programs focusing on improving digital infrastructure in rural areas, providing necessary digital facilities and devices, and offering engaging activities and learning modules can significantly boost participation and digital literacy skills (Abiddin et al., 2022). AI can play a crucial role in creating and delivering these educational programs by developing content that is both accessible and effective. One of the critical advantages of AI in digital literacy education is its ability to offer personalized learning experiences. AI-driven platforms can adapt to individual learner needs, ensuring that even those with limited prior exposure to technology can progress at their own pace (Han, 2020). This personalization extends to various aspects of the learning process, including content delivery, assessment, and feedback. AI can tailor educational content to meet individual student needs, promoting personalized learning and improving student achievement (Dragojević & Lungulov, 2024;Ayala-Pazmiño, 2023). In higher education, AI tools are being integrated into various fields, such as engineering and design, helping students and educators understand and utilize the latest AI opportunities, which is crucial for preparing students for AI-driven professional careers (Āboliņa et al., 2024). Moreover, AI technologies like chatbots and generative AI can simulate human interactions and generate human-like text, which can be particularly beneficial in literacy teaching and learning, making the process more engaging and effective (Kalantzis & Cope, 2023;Adiguzel et al., 2023). The application of AI in digital literacy extends beyond content delivery to assessment and evaluation. AIpowered educational assessment tools can enhance the accuracy and efficiency of assessments, generate personalized feedback, and enable teachers to adapt their teaching strategies to meet the unique needs of each student better, ultimately leading to better educational outcomes (Owan et al., 2023). In the context of English as a Second Language (ESL) classrooms, AI technologies offer promising opportunities to enhance language instruction.",
