        "text": "Data for this study were selected from a large intervention research study (led by the same authors) for a secondary data analysis. Specifically, while previous studies focused on the improvements in students' writing outcomes (e.g., both quantity and quality of written essays) as well as explored how teachers provide feedback on students' writing, the unique focus of this paper was on the use of AI to provide writing feedback (something we have not done before). The data included 34 persuasive student essays, a teacher's completed analytic rubric evaluating the essay, and a teacher's data-driven decisions with instructional feedback in the area of Writing and Reviewing (essays with the teachers' DDDM in the area of Planning were excluded). We purposefully selected essays completed by students with various abilities and needs in different grade levels who struggled with writing and needed the TBGO intervention.",
