      "snippet": {
        "text": "The recent advancement in Artificial Intelligence (AI) has not only aroused great public interest in using the latest tools, including OpenAI's ChatGPT and Microsoft's new Bing, but also received positive feedback from the public. Powered by deep learning models and huge datasets, Generative AI (GenAI) excels over its predecessor in terms of the generation of novel and iterated content, and different multimodal outputs, including text, video, and audio (Chan & Hu, 2023). These GenAI tools, which can generate multimodal and humanlike content in response to various prompts based on deep learning models (Lim et al., 2023;Moorhouse et al., 2024), possess huge potential in the field of education and spark heated discussion in the educational research community. For example, Large Language Models (LLMs), as an epitome of GenAI, allow new and meaningful applications in different fields and are proven to be able to enhance both teaching and learning (Naveed et al., 2023). It has also been observed that LLMs have demonstrated technical proficiency that rivals or surpasses specialized translation tools such as Google Translate and DeepL, which challenges the traditional practices and self-perception of language professionals and prompts an examination of how the field of translation can adapt to the evolving role of GenAI (Lee, 2023). \n\nIn particular, the advent of ChatGPT in November 2022 has been a phenomenal event. It accumulated 100 million users worldwide in just two months after launch, representing the fastest-growing consumer application in history at that time (Hu, 2023), and continues to shock the world through the iteration into GPT-4, making it more creative, collaborative, and accurate (OpenAI, 2024). As an exemplary application of GenAI, the LLM-based ChatGPT, can interact with users in a conversational format, allowing it to provide desired and individualized answers based on natural language inputs. Being fed a large corpus of pre-trained data comprising diverse literary works, scholarly articles, and other text-related materials, ChatGPT harnesses the capabilities of adeptly processing natural language inputs, which is powered by the Transformer algorithm.",
