        "text": "Substantial advancements in deep learning have catalyzed transformative impacts across diverse sectors, particularly within the educational landscape. The integration of artificial intelligence (AI) into educational environments has fundamentally redefined teaching methodologies, enabled \n\nThe associate editor coordinating the review of this manuscript and approving it for publication was Sotirios Goudos . dynamic learning outcome assessments, and fostered personalized learning experiences [1]. Notably, the evolution of generative AI, exemplified by models such as decoderonly, encoder-only, and encoder-decoder frameworks, has significantly advanced natural language processing (NLP) [2]. The launch of OpenAI's ChatGPT in late 2022 demonstrated unprecedented generative capabilities and nuanced contextual understanding, significantly enhancing dialogic interactions over its predecessors [3]. This milestone not only captivated a global audience but also marked a new epoch in AI development. Following this, several commercial platforms such as Flan UL2, Bard, LLaMA, Claude, GPT-4, and ERNIE Bot have emerged, extending productivity gains to sectors such as media, retail, healthcare, and financial services, and propelling the modernization of education. These technologies underscore a broader trend towards the integration of AI tools that are reshaping educational frameworks, enhancing both the delivery and assimilation of knowledge [4]. \n\nThese advancements in generative AI, highlighted by the launch of ChatGPT, have spurred the creation of specialized chatbots like Mathbot, LangBot, CodeHelper, Scite, and Histobot, tailored to meet the diverse requirements of higher education [5]. These chatbots excel in interpreting ambiguous inquiries and generating precise responses, closely aligning with the autonomous learning paradigms of modern educational environments [6]. However, their rapid integration into educational frameworks has sparked significant debate. Concerns include these tools potentially standardizing and depersonalizing education, embedding systemic biases related to race, gender, and social class, diminishing interpersonal communication skills, and negatively influencing learners' values [7], [8], [9]. \n\nNevertheless, a segment of the educational community values chatbots, advocating for their supplementary rather than substitutive role.",
